2025-07-25 15:14:17 | INFO     | api.endpoints.qa:generate_sse:445 - [KNOWLEDGE_DEBUG] 收集到的具体知识来源: [{'id': '15dbe42f-0d54-44a2-86f8-9a4daf257b41', 'content': '问题: 地聚合物（geopolymer）在材料科学中的基本定义是什么？与传统波特兰水泥相比，其主要优势体现在哪些方面？\n答案: A：地聚合物是一种无水泥胶凝材料，通过碱性试剂活化富含铝硅酸盐的工业废弃物（如粉煤灰和矿渣）而制成。与传统波特兰水泥（OPC）生产相比，地聚合物的制造可将碳排放量降低约50%至80%，显著减少温室气体排放，是更可持续的建筑材料选择。', 'title': 'QA: 地聚合物（geopolymer）在材料科学中的基本定义是什么？与传统波特兰水泥相比，其主要优势体现在...', 'score': 1.0, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '982e6f0c-5061-46c5-b967-5973236030c7', 'content': '问题: 地聚合物（Geopolymer）在替代传统波特兰水泥方面具有哪些核心优势？其基本结构特征是什么？\n答案: A：地聚合物被视为波特兰水泥的绿色替代品，主要优势在于其生产过程的碳足迹更低和生产所需能耗更少。此外，它还展现出优异的力学强度、卓越的耐化学性和耐火性能。其基本结构特征是由碱性溶液与富含氧化铝和二氧化硅的粉末前驱体（如粉煤灰、矿渣）反应形成的三维网络结构，其中包含-Si-O-Al-键。', 'title': 'QA: 地聚合物（Geopolymer）在替代传统波特兰水泥方面具有哪些核心优势？其基本结构特征是什么？...', 'score': 1.0, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '311fd6d3-7616-4c46-948d-015861db6a53', 'content': '问题: 地聚物作为一种材料，其主要的优点和缺点是什么？\n答案: A：地聚物是一种无机化合物，可在接近环境温度下固化形成具有耐高温和强度的低碳陶瓷材料。其优点包括相对较高的强度、弹性模量和低收缩性，并且可以替代传统水泥，具有环保效益。然而，其主要缺点是像大多数陶瓷材料一样容易发生脆性断裂。', 'title': 'QA: 地聚物作为一种材料，其主要的优点和缺点是什么？...', 'score': 0.7836068, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'qa_elasticsearch', 'metadata': {}, 'question': '地聚物作为一种材料，其主要的优点和缺点是什么？', 'answer': 'A：地聚物是一种无机化合物，可在接近环境温度下固化形成具有耐高温和强度的低碳陶瓷材料。其优点包括相对较高的强度、弹性模量和低收缩性，并且可以替代传统水泥，具有环保效益。然而，其主要缺点是像大多数陶瓷材料一样容易发生脆性断裂。', 'adopted': True}, {'id': 'e8b1b796-92ee-41bb-9326-e4334cda6904', 'content': '问题: 地聚物材料的基本结构特性是什么？其三维骨架是如何形成的？\n答案: A：地聚物是一种无定形至半结晶的聚合物，其核心结构由硅-氧-铝骨架构成。该三维骨架是通过硅酸盐和铝酸盐物种之间的聚缩合反应形成的。具体而言，它由SiO4和AlO4四面体通过氧桥连接组成，并含有K+、Na+或Ca2+等阳离子来平衡四配位铝（AlIV）所产生的负电荷，形成经验公式为Mn[(SiO2)z-AlO2]n·wH2O的结构。', 'title': 'QA: 地聚物材料的基本结构特性是什么？其三维骨架是如何形成的？...', 'score': 0.7800536, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'qa_elasticsearch', 'metadata': {}, 'question': '地聚物材料的基本结构特性是什么？其三维骨架是如何形成的？', 'answer': 'A：地聚物是一种无定形至半结晶的聚合物，其核心结构由硅-氧-铝骨架构成。该三维骨架是通过硅酸盐和铝酸盐物种之间的聚缩合反应形成的。具体而言，它由SiO4和AlO4四面体通过氧桥连接组成，并含有K+、Na+或Ca2+等阳离子来平衡四配位铝（AlIV）所产生的负电荷，形成经验公式为Mn[(SiO2)z-AlO2]n·wH2O的结构。', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '9cfb5aac-1625-4628-822c-ac5575f3342f', 'content': 'as the reaction proceeds (Bernal et al., 2015) ### 3.4 Phase diagrams for alkali-activated slag-based cements The prediction of several reaction products in the simulated AAS cements is consistent with the bulk chemical composition of the mixes, which generally lie outside the composition envelope of phase-pure C-(N-)A-S-H gel (Figure 8). Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006 Further analysis of AAS cement chemistry is performed by simulating phase diagrams at a fixed slag reaction extent of ${60}\\%$ , a constant amount of ${\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\mathrm{\\;S}$ (equivalent in $\\mathrm{S}$ content to a slag composition of 2 mass% ${\\mathrm{{SO}}}_{3}$ , which is taken as a representative value of $\\mathrm{S}$ content in slags studied in the literature Ben Haha et al., 2011a; Bernal et al., 2014b. Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。 Richardson et al., 1994; Shi et al., 2006;) and slag compositions of either 30 or ${40}\\mathrm{{mass}}\\% {\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , with the remaining chemical composition specified in terms of $\\mathrm{{CaO}},{\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3}$ and $\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ only. The $\\mathrm{{CaO}}$ - ${\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3} - \\mathrm{{MgO}}$ composition range selected here was chosen to represent the bulk chemical composition range relevant to AAS-based cements.\n![0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg](images/0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg)', 'title': '', 'score': 0.05, 'source_type': 'document', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'extra': None, 'headings': [], 'strategy': 'semantic', 'page_number': [1], 'dual_vector_metadata': "{'general_text': 'as the reaction proceeds (Bernal et al., 2015) ### 3.4 Phase diagrams for alkali-activated slag-based cements The prediction of several reaction products in the simulated AAS cements is consistent with the bulk chemical composition of the mixes, which generally lie outside the composition envelope of phase-pure C-(N-)A-S-H gel (Figure 8). Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006 Further analysis of AAS cement chemistry is performed by simulating phase diagrams at a fixed slag reaction extent of ${60}\\\\%$ , a constant amount of ${\\\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;S}$ (equivalent in $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content to a slag composition of 2 mass% ${\\\\mathrm{{SO}}}_{3}$ , which is taken as a representative value of $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content in slags studied in the literature Ben Haha et al., 2011a; Bernal et al., 2014b. Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。 Richardson et al., 1994; Shi et al., 2006;) and slag compositions of either 30 or ${40}\\\\mathrm{{mass}}\\\\% {\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , with the remaining chemical composition specified in terms of $\\\\mathrm{{CaO}},{\\\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{O}}_{3}$ and $\\\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ only. The $\\\\mathrm{{CaO}}$ - ${\\\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{O}}_{3} - \\\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ composition range selected here was chosen to represent the bulk chemical composition range relevant to AAS-based cements.\\n![0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg](images/0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg)', 'domain_text': 'as the reaction proceeds (Bernal et al., 2015) ### 3.4 Phase diagrams for alkali-activated slag-based cements The prediction of several reaction products in the simulated AAS cements is consistent with the bulk chemical composition of the mixes, which generally lie outside the composition envelope of phase-pure C-(N-)A-S-H gel (Figure 8). Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006 Further analysis of AAS cement chemistry is performed by simulating phase diagrams at a fixed slag reaction extent of ${60}\\\\%$ , a constant amount of ${\\\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;S}$ (equivalent in $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content to a slag composition of 2 mass% ${\\\\mathrm{{SO}}}_{3}$ , which is taken as a representative value of $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content in slags studied in the literature Ben Haha et al., 2011a; Bernal et al., 2014b. Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。 Richardson et al., 1994; Shi et al., 2006;) and slag compositions of either 30 or ${40}\\\\mathrm{{mass}}\\\\% {\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , with the remaining chemical composition s', 'original_tokens': 539, 'general_tokens': 539, 'domain_tokens': 421, 'text_adapted': True, 'tokenizer_used': 'matbert_tokenizer_for_domain'}"}, 'highlights': {'content': ['Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而<mark>定</mark>。']}, 'adopted': True}]
